        "instructions": "### Goal\nImplement the three load-balancing selection strategies (`RoundRobin.pick`, `LeastConnections.pick`, `PowerOfTwoChoices.pick`) and RFC 9110 §7.6.1 hop-by-hop header stripping (`stripHopByHop`).\n\n### Algorithm & Invariants\n1. **`stripHopByHop(headers)`**:\n   - Clone `headers` so the caller's object is not mutated.\n   - Parse `headers.connection` (comma-separated header names, trimmed and lowercased).\n   - Delete every header in `HOP_BY_HOP` **and** every header listed dynamically in `Connection`.\n2. **`RoundRobin.pick(eligible)`**:\n   - Return `eligible[this.next % eligible.length]` and advance `this.next = (this.next + 1) % 1e9`.\n3. **`LeastConnections.pick(eligible)`**:\n   - Start scanning at rotating index `start = this.offset++ % n` so ties are broken fairly across backends instead of always hammering index `0`.\n   - Pick the backend with the strictly smallest `b.active` count.\n4. **`PowerOfTwoChoices.pick(eligible)`**:\n   - If `eligible.length === 1`, return `eligible[0]`.\n   - Sample index `i = Math.floor(this.rng() * n)` and a distinct second index `j = Math.floor(this.rng() * (n - 1))` (increment `j` if `j >= i`).\n   - Return `b.active < a.active ? b : a` (breaking ties in favor of the first sample `a`).",
