        "instructions": "### Goal\nImplement `_recordResult(b, ok)` to passively eject failing backends while protecting the fleet via `maxEjectionPercent`.\n\n### Algorithm & Invariants\n1. **Success resets failure streak**:\n   - If `ok` is true, set `b.consecutiveFailures = 0` and return immediately.\n2. **Failure threshold check**:\n   - Increment `b.consecutiveFailures++`. If `b.consecutiveFailures < this.outlier.consecutiveFailures`, return.\n   - Check `const t = this.now()`; if `t < b.ejectedUntil`, the backend is already ejected—return.\n3. **Panic threshold (`maxEjectionPercent`)**:\n   - Count currently ejected backends: `const ejected = this.backends.filter((x) => t < x.ejectedUntil).length`.\n   - If `((ejected + 1) / this.backends.length) * 100 > this.outlier.maxEjectionPercent`, refuse to eject so a cascading downstream issue never takes down 100% of the fleet.\n4. **Eject with linear/exponential multiplier**:\n   - Increment `b.ejections++`, set `b.ejectedUntil = t + this.outlier.baseEjectionMs * b.ejections`, and reset `b.consecutiveFailures = 0`.",
