        "concept": "Lossless Precision Reduction (p -> q) & Commutative Sketch Union",
        "instructions": "Implement `HyperLogLog.withPrecision(q)` in `hll.js` to fold a precision-`p` sketch down to a coarser precision `q <= p`. For each non-zero register `j` with rank `r`, split `j` into `nj = j >>> d` and `low = j & ((1 << d) - 1)` where `d = p - q`. Compute the folded rank `nr = low !== 0 ? Math.clz32(low) - (32 - d) + 1 : d + r` and take the max in `out.registers[nj]`.",
